# Line-ending policy for this DSH port.
#
# Upstream's own rule, preserved verbatim:
#
#   Shell scripts MUST stay LF, even on Windows checkouts. The PreToolUse hook
#   launcher (hooks/run_guard.sh) and the SessionStart announce hook
#   (scripts/announce-ars-loaded.sh) are executed via Git Bash on Windows; a CRLF
#   checkout would break them on the hot path (#454). Scope the rule to *.sh so
#   existing line-ending behavior for other files is untouched.
#
*.sh text eol=lf

# Port addition. Upstream leaves non-`*.sh` files to `text=auto`, so a Windows
# checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites every Markdown/Python/JSON file to
# CRLF. That silently breaks two bundled mechanisms, which is why this port pins
# LF for the whole tree instead:
#
#   * `scripts/check_pipeline_boundary_semantics.py` pins five pipeline surfaces
#     by WHOLE-FILE sha256, so its locks must not depend on the checkout's
#     line-ending configuration.
#   * `scripts/check_tools_allowlist.py` reads the agents' frozen `tools:` line
#     without universal-newline translation on purpose, so a CRLF file fires it.
#
# Keeping the committed bytes LF makes those checks meaningful on every platform
# and keeps the content locks stable across re-checkouts.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries are never line-ending-converted.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.ttc   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.exe   binary
*.dll   binary
*.pyc   binary
